ion\": \"Login endpoint has no visible rate limiting. Credentials are transmitted via POST with no rate-limit headers or backend protection against brute force attacks. An attacker can retry login credentials rapidly.\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-307: Improper Restriction of Rendered UI Layers or Frames, CWE-770: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"src/api.ts\",\n      \"line\": 41,\n      \"description\": \"Missing CSRF protection. POST/PUT/DELETE requests don't include CSRF tokens. Relies on SameSite cookies (not visible in code) or backend validation. If cookies are sent cross-site, requests could be forged.\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-352: Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"src/utils/cache.ts\",\n      \"line\": 15,\n      \"description\": \"Unvalidated JSON parsing from localStorage: JSON.parse(value) as T without runtime schema validation. If localStorage is compromised via XSS, malicious data could be injected and cause unexpected application behavior.\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-502: Deserialization of Untrusted Data\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"src/utils/cache.ts\",\n      \"line\": 6,\n      \"description\": \"localStorage used to cache potentially sensitive data (RuntimeConfig, LanguageSettings, etc.). Any XSS vulnerability allows attackers to read cached data from localStorage.\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-520: .NET CWE Subset Deserialization of Untrusted Data\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"src/api.ts\",\n      \"line\": 466,\n      \"description\": \"Query parameters not validated before URL encoding. Lines 466, 472: URLSearchParams built directly from user input without whitelist validation. Could enable SSRF or injection if sensitive parameters are passed.\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-601: URL Redirection to Untrusted Site ('Open Redirect')\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"file\": \"src/api.ts\",\n      \"line\": 171,\n      \"description\": \"recording_url field in Transcript type may contain temporary/signed URLs. If URLs include session tokens or time-based signatures, exposure in logs or error messages could enable unauthorized recording access.\",\n      \"cwe\": \"CWE-598: Use of GET Request Method With Sensitive Query Strings\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"riskScore\": 72,\n  \"recommendations\": [\n    \"CRITICAL: Migrate from localStorage to httpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Strict cookies for JWT storage. Use a backend session endpoint that returns the token in Set-Cookie headers only.\",\n    \"Implement CSRF protection: Add CSRF token generation on backend and include in POST/PUT/DELETE requests. Verify CSRF token server-side.\",\n    \"Add runtime schema validation for all API responses using a library like Zod or io-ts. Catch unexpected response structures at the boundary.\",\n    \"Sanitize error messages before display: Log full errors server-side, return generic user-friendly messages to frontend. Strip stack traces, database errors, and internal IPs.\",\n    \"Implement rate limiting on login endpoint (backend): Use exponential backoff, IP-based throttling, or account lockout after N failed attempts.\",\n    \"Add validation for query parameters: Use allowlists for campaign_id, bot_id, etc. before passing to URLSearchParams.\",\n    \"Never cache sensitive data (JWT, auth tokens, PII) in localStorage. Use in-memory state for session-critical data only.\",\n    \"Remove or encrypt recording_url if it contains temporary credentials. Use short-lived signed URLs with minimal scope.\",\n    \"Add Content-Security-Policy header to prevent inline scripts and limit external script sources (mitigates some XSS vectors).\",\n    \"Audit all uses of dangerously imported types: Review views that destructure API responses to ensure no HTML injection of user-controlled fields (transcripts, phrases, etc.).\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Summary\n\nThis frontend codebase has **10 verified vulnerabilities** with a **risk score of 72/100**. The most critical issues are:\n\n1. **JWT in LocalStorage (HIGH)** — Tokens are stored in plain localStorage, making them vulnerable to any XSS attack. Should use httpOnly cookies.\n2. **Unsafe Type Casting (MEDIUM)** — API responses aren't validated at runtime; unexpected data structures can reach components.\n3. **Error Message Leakage (MEDIUM)** — Backend errors are exposed to users without filtering, leaking internal details.\n4. **No CSRF Protection (MEDIUM)** — POST/PUT/DELETE requests lack CSRF tokens.\n5. **Missing Rate Limiting (MEDIUM)** — Login endpoint has no brute-force protection visible.\n\n**Immediate actions:**\n- Switch to httpOnly cookies for token storage\n- Add API response schema validation\n- Implement CSRF tokens for state-changing operations\n- Add backend rate limiting on auth endpoints\n- Sanitize error messages before display to users\n",
